# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# OZKAFE ANASSA — Vercel & Supabase Environment Configuration
# 100% Free Tier Setup
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# 1. Supabase Project Settings (from Supabase Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API)
# Note: The application connects to Supabase entirely server-side from Vercel.
# Client devices in India connect only to your Vercel URL, completely bypassing Indian ISP DNS blocks!
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-supabase-anon-key
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-supabase-service-role-key

# 2. Public URLs (Optional)
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://your-anassa-app.vercel.app

# 3. Proxy Configuration (Auto-configured — no changes needed)
# The proxy system is built into the app and activates automatically:
#   - Custom fetch wrapper: retry + exponential back-off + timeout
#   - Edge rewrites: /_supabase/* -> Supabase REST/Auth/Storage APIs
#   - API proxy route: /api/supabase-proxy/* (fallback path)
#   - Vercel region: iad1 (US East) — avoids Indian ISP DNS blocks
# See /api/health for real-time proxy diagnostics.
